R-CM4 R-CM19 R-SP4 R-SP14 R-SP11 R-NI2 R-NM7 R-NR4 R-PD9 R-SO7 R-PH8 R-SE7 R-DT5 R-I5 R-LF4 R-HF1 R-EV22 (slice 009, Q2, Q3): the command code of `update` with the fake Fx, 5 runs on one project (`u1`: a platform acme/pfx 0.1.0, json 2.0.0, parser 1.0.0, and talon.toml with the key `lex` that the header lacks).
The calls of one run fix the order of Update.run!: args, env, clock, cwd, the project (canonical, list_dirs, read_files), canonical of the project file and the record in projects.json. With `-i`: the picker comes next (`tty` once, one `read_files` call of `Resolve.picks!`, then the ask loop), and only after it the compiler (`programs`, `roc version`) and the flow. A run that stops in the picker has made no compiler call.
Run 1: `update -i --json` is non-interactive mode, also with a tty: a picker has no person (R-NM7, R-NI2), exit 2 and the envelope. No tty call, no read of the header, no compiler call. Run 2: the person types `9` (Invalid: the list has 3 items, the picker asks again) and then `1 3`: json and pf are picked (R-SP4: the flow is `update json pf`). The platform moves, so there is the notice (R-SE7), and the line R-DT5.
The list is on stderr, once (R-NR1). Run 3: the person presses Enter: nothing is picked, the line `nothing picked`, exit 0, no compiler call and no flow. Run 4: `update` with no name moves parser only (the others are at the newest release in range). Q3: the key `lex` has no effect, so there is no index call for acme/lex and no `lex` entry (R-I5: only `install` adds it). Run 5: the person is gone (the answers are used up, `ask!` gives the end of input): the picker is a usage failure like the non-interactive one (exit 2, R-NM7), with the list shown and nothing written.
